      "message": "This is glorious. Just so I understand fully - we can\u0027t just return SkBlender::Mode() (vs. wrapping in the pass-through runtime blender), because if we\u0027re using this to replace the actual blend on the paint - that would send us back to fixed-function blending? In any other context (eg, in blend image filter, as a blender child of another runtime effect) - the wrapper doesn\u0027t do much? Maybe just add a comment that says that the wrapper ensures that in all contexts, this is forcing us to do shader-based blending?",
